WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.650
Trust is the most precious commodity to the
Mandalorian, and in chapter 5 of his Disney+

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.300
series, what little trust he can invest pays
few dividends.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.360
A brief layover on the most familiar of planets
Tatooine ends with Mando getting little more

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.700
than he started with, beyond a fixed ship
and a blaster-scorched chestplate.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.440
The biggest twist occurred during the last
moments, so beware: we're about to enter major

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.580
spoiler territory.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:29.880
In The Mandalorian's fifth chapter, entitled
"The Gunslinger," we saw Toro Calican seemingly

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.840
kill Fennec Shand after she attempts to manipulate
him into releasing her and accompanying her

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.040
back to one of Tatooine's spaceport cities,
Mos Espa.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:42.371
At first, we consider that maybe she was just
stunned, and will eventually wake up, but

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.820
several shots cut back to her to underline
that yes, Shand is most likely dead.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:51.400
In the last five seconds of the episode, black
boots and a cape approach Shand's body.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:52.520
Who could it be?

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:57.580
After Chapter 4's heavy focus on Mando and
his personal motivations, chapter 5 is more

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:01.790
interested in stepping back perspective to
be less about him and more about the greater

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.300
circumstances of the world in which he lives.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:08.700
Mando may be its center, but the universe
that orbits around him sometimes takes greater

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.000
precedence, leaving him to be an actor within
it.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.530
The galaxy is getting bigger and bigger with
each new episode of The Mandalorian, and Mando

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:17.240
is slowly losing control of it.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.259
The apparent death of Fennec Shand and the
aftermath of the incident made up the biggest

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:22.820
plot twist of episode 5.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:27.660
Ming-Na Wen is one of the most recognizable
actors who was publicly attached to The Mandalorian

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:31.460
prior to its release, but we still don't know
much about her role on the show.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:36.259
Secrecy around the series has remained tight,
we don't know exactly how many episodes Wen

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:37.520
is supposed to appear on.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:42.200
After all, she's got one heck of a backstory,
and it'd be a shame to just leave it all behind

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.280
after one show.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.680
"Fennec Shand is an elite mercenary.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:50.640
She made her name killing for all the top
crime syndicates — including the Hutts."

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:55.859
Also, Star Wars has a history of bringing
characters we thought were dead back to life,

00:01:55.859 --> 00:02:00.299
sometimes going through a whole lot of hoops
to justify a hero or villain's continuing

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:00.800
survival.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:05.320
The obvious question is this: Who's the dude
swaggering on up to Shand's body?

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:09.760
Our best guess is that it's whomever she was
supposed to meet with back at Mos Espa.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:13.060
Remember, that was the exact deal she pitched
to Calican:

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:17.180
"Take me to it, and I can pay you double the
price on my head."

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.440
But why was Shand on Tatooine at all?

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:23.720
From the information Calican presented, she's
been using the planet as a hideout.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.670
We don't see Shand in the middle of some other
job out in the desert wilds, either.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.180
Who is she going to meet while on the run
that's going to pay her?

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:36.100
Chapter 5 takes the time to explicitly mention
that the New Republic has cut off a lot of

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:40.000
Shand's usual contractors by defeating the
Empire and its subsidiaries.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.360
Mando is taking commissions while on the run,
too, and Chapter 5's whole premise is built

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:45.360
around this need.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:50.000
Maybe Shand picked up the job that will make
her flush and able to get off-world at last.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.660
However, Shand's an assassin.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:56.620
Mando kills people as necessary for cash,
but his general job description is to bring

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:01.380
them in alive and up until recently, that
was done according to a code of ethics required

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.100
by the guild.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:06.340
Assassins have different, and far less patient
contractors.

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:10.700
It's possible that the aerial dogfight that
opens the episode and Shand being on Tatooine

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:11.360
are related.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.920
Does the twist lie in the planet being a honeypot
to ground Mando?

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:19.120
Was Shand somehow contracted to separate Mando
from the Child and kill him?

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:24.740
She clearly prioritizes killing Mando during
the fight so much so that Calican easily sneak

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:28.440
up on her and threaten to shoot, which is
pretty sloppy on her behalf.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.900
That possibility might be a little contrived,
but the fact that Shand is aware of everything

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.260
that happened at Nevarro is a bit suspicious.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:40.380
"I hear things didn't go so well there but
it looks like you got off easy."

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:44.160
The order in which she pitches her deals to
Calican is telling, too.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:48.650
She tries to get herself free without mentioning
the high price attached to Mando, but later

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:52.640
feels forced to mention the possibility of
splitting the reward for killing Mando.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:56.510
She presents this meeting at which she'll
be paid and the bounty attached to Mando as

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:59.730
two separate things, but there's no guarantee
that's true.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:03.959
If so, Shand definitely came out the losing
end in this bargain, and there would be severe

00:04:03.959 --> 00:04:08.790
consequences for her, if she's still alive,
as well as whomever contracted her, and, of

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.420
course, Mando and the Child.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:15.280
How any of this ties back to Mando is completely
inscrutable for the moment, but we know it'll

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:19.689
all come together eventually, regardless of
whether or not Fennec Shand is alive.

